# Cursor Rules for Svelte + TypeScript Project

## Project Context
This is a Svelte 5 project using TypeScript, Vite, and Tailwind CSS.

## Code Style & Best Practices

### TypeScript
- Use TypeScript for all `.ts` and `.svelte` files
- Prefer explicit types over `any`
- Use type inference where it improves readability
- Follow the existing TypeScript configuration in `tsconfig.json` and `tsconfig.app.json`

### Svelte
- Use Svelte 5 runes syntax (`$state`, `$derived`, `$effect`, etc.)
- Prefer composition over complex component hierarchies
- Keep components focused and single-purpose
- Use TypeScript in `<script lang="ts">` blocks
- Follow Svelte naming conventions (PascalCase for components)

### Styling
- Use Tailwind CSS utility classes for styling
- Keep component-specific styles in `<style>` blocks when needed
- Prefer Tailwind classes over custom CSS when possible

### File Organization
- Place reusable components in `src/lib/`
- Keep page-level components in `src/`
- Use clear, descriptive file names matching component names

### Code Quality
- Write clean, readable, and maintainable code
- Add comments for complex logic or non-obvious decisions
- Keep functions small and focused
- Prefer early returns for better readability

### Git & Version Control
- Write meaningful commit messages
- Don't commit generated files or dependencies
- Keep commits focused and atomic

## Component Structure

/[module-name]
  |-- index.ts
  |-- [module-name].svelte
  |-- [module-name].types.ts
  |-- [module-name].constants.ts
  |-- [module-name].utils.ts

### Index File
- The index always has the following structure:
  ```ts
  export { default as [ModuleName] } from './[module-name].svelte';
  export * from './[module-name].types';
  export * from './[module-name].constants';
  export * from './[module-name].utils';
  ```

### Component File
- The component file always has the following structure:
  ```svelte
  <script lang="ts">
    import type { MyComponentProps } from './[module-name].types';

    let { ... }: MyComponentProps = $props();
  </script>

  ... component code ...
  ```

### Types File
- The types file always has the following structure:
  ```ts
  export type MyComponentProps = {
    ... component props types ...
  };
  ```

### Constants File
- The constants file always has the following structure:
  ```ts
  export const MY_CONSTANT = 'my constant';
  ```

### Utils File
- The utils file always has the following structure:
  ```ts
  export const myUtil = () => {
    ... utility function ...
  };
  ```

## Development Workflow
- Use `npm run dev` for development
- Use `npm run check` to verify TypeScript and Svelte types
- Use `npm run build` to create production builds
